id     = "time-signals-reduced"
about  = """design.md "Runtime changes these need" 7 and spec.md 6.6: with the
desktop's reduced-motion setting on, time signals stop. #dot sways on
`x: 4 * wave(1s)` and breathes on `opacity: 0.6 + 0.4 * wave(2s)`, #spin
turns on `rotate: t * 90deg`; once motion is reduced their clocks stand at
t = 0 (time.rs `TimeContext::frozen`): the bar rests, and each stands
where the reduced-motion twin, frozen from the start, draws it. A
time-driven node mounted while motion is reduced stands still too."""
screen = { width = 300, scale = 1.0 }

=== shell.strand
state more = false
bar Top {
  height: 30
  row { id: status; height: 24; gap: 6; align: center
    box { id: dot; width: 10; height: 10; bg: #ff0000
          x: 4 * wave(1s); opacity: 0.6 + 0.4 * wave(2s) }
    box { id: spin; width: 12; height: 12; bg: #00ff00; rotate: t * 90deg }
    if more {
      box { id: late; width: 12; height: 12; bg: #ffff00; rotate: t * 45deg }
    }
    box { id: steady; width: 20; height: 12; bg: #0000ff }
  }
}

=== steps
frames 40
expect moves #dot x
expect moves #dot opacity
expect moves #spin w
mark reduce
reduce-motion on
rest
mark still
frames 30
expect still #dot
expect still #dot opacity
expect still #spin
mark mount
set more true
rest
frames 30
expect still #late from +2
expect still #spin
